.research/260729_curator-go-to-csk-parity-delta.md:145:`protocol/core.md` §4.2.1 defines exactly one execution policy for protocol 1.0 and states that every conforming manager MUST implement `manager-worker-v1` **on macOS and Windows**. The policy identity is a normative cache, receipt, marker, and claim input, never a package-visible option or operator preference. The fixed process graph is: manager parent → identity-verified manager-owned worker → fingerprinted `<GOROOT>/bin/go` → fingerprinted regular executables below `<GOROOT>/pkg/tool/<GOHOSTOS>_<GOHOSTARCH>/`.
