json rules hold: schema-valid-is-not-qualified, driver-platform-subset, no-generic-driver over exactly go-repository-v1 and go-v1, no-unevidenced-platform, linux excluded until TASK-260728-1skseh, and macos and windows pending-downstream-native-evidence. No conformance claim is emitted by this task. Legacy rc.3 vectors remain green. Tests against the exact caller-supplied candidate suite and strict mypy pass, the candidate revision and full manifest digest are recorded as non-release evidence, and no committed curator-spec pin or release claim changes.
.task-board/EPIC-260720-21aq1i_declarative-compiled-builds/STORY-260720-3plyvy_curator-go-build-driver/TASK-260720-1zntv0_implement-go-v1-preflight-and-build/README.md:7:Continue in internal/godriver using the trusted session and frozen build source. Use an identity-verified manager-owned worker boundary where needed; set CWD to canonical source_dir; pass only manager-defined argv and a fixed offline environment; mark snapshot/vendor inputs read-only where supported; write only manager-created operation-private Go cache, temp, telemetry and output roots by construction; bound time, captured output and artifact size; apply every reviewed native process-tree, memory, filesystem and network control available on the host; verify source/toolchain identities after execution; and report capabilities honestly. Parse the complete fixed go list stream, validate every package input, reject cgo/native/workspace/PGO/generator/external-link/input escapes, build with the normative internal-link argv and never execute the artifact. Do not publish caches, write markers or mutate live installs. The portable profile must not claim the six hardened guarantees tracked by STORY-260728-327soo and must not fail solely because a host lacks those hardened primitives.
.task-board/EPIC-260720-21aq1i_declarative-compiled-builds/STORY-260720-3plyvy_curator-go-build-driver/TASK-260720-1zntv0_implement-go-v1-preflight-and-build/progress.md:78:2026-07-27 solution-architecture finding: the direct Go os/exec graph cannot install the required native filesystem/network/process/resource controls before compiler execution. Of the two documented contracts, recommend one identity-verified manager-owned worker plus a fail-closed capability-gated hardened Linux profile; current macOS and Windows profiles must reject before worker/Go. Retain go-v1 before unreleased rc.4 only with an explicit manager-worker-v1 cache/receipt policy revision. Justified gap self-check covered protocol/core §4.2, profiles/manager §§2.2–2.4, SECURITY compile-only/compiler-input, decision 0004, closed policy schema, accepted contract research, and rejected/out-of-scope alternatives: the fixed worker is not package-selected, but the graph change requires human authorization. No new board tasks were created because existing spec, Curator, csk, and downstream owners are the smallest traceable decomposition and implementation must not be presumed before authorization. Exact decision and task/CI map are attached in TASK-260720-1zntv0_host-execution-decision.md.
